      "Honest limits",
      "Compression is a trade, not a magic trick. Push quality too low and you will see it: blocky patches in skies, smeared text in screenshots, halos around sharp edges. The slider gives you control, but no setting can make a 200 KB file hold the detail of a 10 MB original.",
      "Enlarging is outside the tool's job entirely. Compression can only work with the pixels you have; a small, blurry photo will not become a large, sharp one. Likewise, a heavily compressed image cannot have its lost detail recovered later — keep your originals backed up before you batch-process anything you care about.",
