      "Honest limits",
      "A summarizer selects; it does not understand. It cannot tell you whether an argument is sound, whether a statistic is trustworthy, or whether the author's conclusion actually follows from the evidence. If the original text is muddled, the summary will be a shorter muddle. It also cannot add context — background knowledge the author assumed stays assumed.",
      "Length modes are a blunt instrument. Some documents have one crucial sentence buried in an otherwise weak paragraph, and frequency-based scoring can miss it. For high-stakes material — legal text, medical guidance, anything you will be examined or judged on — treat the summary as a navigation aid and read the important sections in full.",
