      "Ask any new creator what stops their short videos and the answer is rarely the footage. It is everything around the footage: a title that says nothing, a caption written in four seconds, hashtags copied from somebody else's post, and — for anyone re-editing clips — an ugly watermark sitting in the corner that screams 'borrowed'. Platforms like YouTube Shorts, TikTok and Instagram Reels give a video seconds to earn a swipe-past or a watch, and the packaging decides much of that before a single frame plays.",
